  "question": {
    "text": "If $a$ and $c$ are positive real numbers and the ellipse $\\frac{x^2}{4 c^2}+\\frac{y^2}{c^2}=1$ has four distinct points ir common with the circle $x^2+y^2=9 a^2$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eX2cA",
      "text": "\n$9 a c-9 a^2-2 c^2 < 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qXp7Q",
      "text": "\n$6 a c+9 a^2-2 c^2 < 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "FLHb2",
      "text": "\n$9 a c-9 a^2-2 c^2>0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "3zO7M",
      "text": "\n$6 a c+9 a^2-2 c^2>0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Radius $=3 a$\nLength of major axis $=4 c$\nNow, (Radius $) < $ (Half of the length of major axis)\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& 3 a < 2 c \\\\\n& 9 a^2 < 4 c^2 \\\\\n& 9 a c-9 a^2>9 a c-4 c^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/xQbpNBJ_bhsM-pFAeuKc9P2DiJPOeYBzDnhNZmv5ZHM.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n$9 a c-9 a^2-2 c^2>9 a c-6 c^2$\nAgain $3 a < 2 c$\n$\\Rightarrow 9 a c < 6 c^2$\n$\\Rightarrow 9 a c-6 c^2 < 0$\nFrom (i) and (ii),\n$9 a c-9 a^2-2 c^2>0$",
    "image": null
  },
